1a:["$","p","p-2",{"children":["Use ",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"timeouts"}]," at every network call so a stuck dependency does not occupy a worker indefinitely. Allow a little margin between the dependency timeout, the worker's overall deadline, and the broker visibility lease. A circuit breaker can temporarily stop calls to a clearly failing dependency, but a queued job still needs a later retry or explicit failure outcome."]}]
1b:["$","h2","h2-1",{"id":"bound-the-retry-budget","children":"Bound the retry budget"}]
1c:["$","p","p-3",{"children":"One policy might attempt after about 0, 2, 6, and 14 seconds, with jitter, then quarantine the job. The numbers are illustrative; derive them from the dependency's recovery behavior and the user's completion promise. Jitter spreads retries from many workers so they do not all strike a recovering service together. Avoid stacking independent SDK, worker, and broker retries without counting their combined attempts."}]
1d:["$","p","p-4",{"children":["Keep a ",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"deadline"}]," or maximum elapsed time as well as an attempt limit. A four-attempt policy that stretches beyond the user's useful window is not reliable delivery. Record attempt count, last error class, and next eligible time without leaking document content into logs."]}]
