23:["$","p","p-7",{"children":"A DLQ preserves messages that repeatedly fail so operators can inspect them without blocking healthy work. It is not a substitute for a user-facing failure state. For each quarantined export, correlate the message to its operation and record a safe reason. Provide a controlled replay procedure: fix the cause, inspect whether the effect already happened, choose one message or a bounded batch, replay with the same operation ID, and observe the outcome. Preserve redrive history so a poison message does not loop forever."}]
